@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Game Controls";
}

<h1>Game Controls</h1>

<p>
    You can click (or tap) on a tile in your rack to select it. Once selected it will be highlighted with a red border. You can then click (or tap) on an available space on the board. Alternatively; if you use a mouse you can drag and drop tiles to and from the board.
</p>

<hr/>
<h2>Buttons</h2>
<p>

</p>

<ul style="list-style-type: none;">
    <li>
        <img src="~/img/control-tilebag.PNG"/> If enabled in your game you can click this to see the remaining tiles.
        <hr/>
    </li>
    <li>
        <img src="~/img/control-recalltiles.PNG"/> This button will recall your tiles from the board to your rack.
        <hr/>
    </li>
    <li>
        <img src="~/img/control-shuffle.PNG"/> This button will shuffle the tiles in your rack.
        <hr/>
    </li>
    <li>
        <img src="~/img/control-skipturn.PNG"/> This button will skip your turn. You will be asked to confirm the action when clicking.
        <hr/>
    </li>
    <li>
        <img src="~/img/control-exchangetiles.PNG"/> This button will allow you to exchange tiles. You will be asked to confirm the action when clicking.
    </li>
</ul>